WHY THIS IS A SEPARATE FILE, AND WHY IT MUST STAY ONE
-----------------------------------------------------
DVRef placed its reflector data under CC BY 4.0 in its "Accessing DVRef Data"
announcement of 2026-08-04, explicitly permitting mirroring, reformatting,
commercial use, and the creation of "host files, APIs, directories, and other
services".

CC BY 4.0 section 2(a)(5)(B) forbids a redistributor from offering or imposing
"any additional or different terms or conditions on ... the Licensed Material
if doing so restricts exercise of the Licensed Rights". The rest of hamcall-db
is CC BY-NC 4.0 — non-commercial. Merging this reflector data into those
artifacts would impose a non-commercial restriction that CC BY 4.0 grants away,
so it would be a LICENSE VIOLATION, not merely untidy bookkeeping.

This is the same segregation discipline the project applies to the
OpenStreetMap-derived park grids (see LICENSE-ODbL), pointing the other way:
there the upstream is MORE restrictive than the project, here it is LESS.

Do not co-locate or merge these files into the CC BY-NC artifacts.

